# memory_gap_huge_task: A task of 32 GiB (0x800000000, the in-process maximum) at depth 3, with leaves only for its first eight VA pages (object list, records, command buffers) and three far pages: the last page of the first second-level table's range (VA page 4095), the first of the next (4096), and the task's very last page (2^21 - 1). A buffer over pages 4095 and 4096 crosses from one last-level table to the next; one over the last page ends exactly at the task's end. Fills of both land in every setup; in the blocks setup the host task is a 32 GiB reservation and only the pages used are mapped into it.
